@crew chen-carmen
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hi. Chen, Watch. Sorry, I was miles away. Literally. About forty light years.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hey, {me}. I was just telling my grandmother about you. Only good things.
- Hello, {me}. Is it Tuesday? It feels like a Tuesday.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. You're on my list of good things aboard. Near the top.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Lovely day. Sang all the way through patrol. In my head. Mostly.
? mood:low
- Restless. I've walked Deck 4 three times. It hasn't changed.
== near
? deck:3 act:free
- This bench is mine. Well, I sit on it. That's how benches work.   #funny
? weekday:sat|sun act:free
- Recording a message for my grandmother on Lisk. Say hello? She'll love it.
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I send voice messages to my grandmother on Lisk. They're long. She says too short.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- My bench in the garden. Leaves above, pumps humming. I can think there.
